<p>Beyond the e-Way Bill, the Lorry Receipt (LR) or Bilty serves as the primary contract of carriage. An IBA-approved LR is essential because it acts as the title document for your goods during transit. It details the sender, receiver, itemization, and the exact terms of liability.</p>
<p>Without a properly stamped IBA-compliant LR, you may face difficulties filing claims if damage occurs. This document is the backbone of professional <strong>household moving and storage</strong> operations, bridging the gap between pickup and delivery.</p>
<p>Physical documentation alone does not mitigate risk; comprehensive insurance is the final line of defense. For high-value contents, standard transit cover is insufficient. Opt for comprehensive 100% declared-value IRDAI marine transit insurance.</p>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">This policy specifically covers accidental collision, overturning, fire, and unforeseen delays that may lead to spoilage or damage.</p>
