      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">The final delivery and uncrating protocol at Bhadrak is a structured, step‑by‑step operation that guarantees every item arrives in perfect condition, functions as intended, and is positioned exactly where it belongs.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>By adhering to a daylight verification, rigorous testing, meticulous placement, and prompt cleanup, the team minimizes errors, protects assets, and delivers a professional finish that meets both safety standards and client expectations.</span></li></ul>

<ul>
<li><strong>Daylight delivery verification against the original inventory bilty</strong>
    <ul>
        <li>All pallets and crates are inspected immediately upon arrival under natural light to detect any visible damage, discoloration, or missing components.</li>
        <li>The on‑site supervisor cross‑checks each item with the inventory bilty, marking off quantities, serial numbers, and model identifiers in real time.</li>
        <li>Discrepancies are recorded on a discrepancy report, photographed, and communicated to the logistics coordinator within 15 minutes to initiate corrective action.</li>
        <li>Verified items receive a temporary “cleared” tag, allowing them to proceed to the testing zone without delay.</li>
    </ul>
</li>

<li><strong>Testing of electrical and mechanical items</strong>
    <ul>
        <li>Each electrical unit is plugged into a dedicated test circuit equipped with surge protection and voltage monitoring.</li>
        <li>Functional checks include power‑on verification, indicator lights, control panel response, and basic performance metrics as defined in the manufacturer’s test sheet.</li>
        <li>Mechanical components undergo a visual inspection for alignment, moving parts lubrication, and a short operational run to confirm smooth motion and absence of abnormal noises.</li>
        <li>All test results are logged on a digital checklist; any item that fails is isolated, labeled “re‑work required,” and routed back to the supplier or maintenance team.</li>
    </ul>
</li>

<li><strong>Clean furniture placement</strong>
    <ul>
        <li>Approved items are moved using soft‑tipped dollies and protective pads to avoid floor scratches.</li>
        <li>Each piece is positioned according to the floor‑plan layout, ensuring proper orientation, clearance, and ergonomic alignment.</li>
        <li>Surface cleaning is performed with a lint‑free cloth and a mild, non‑abrasive cleaner before final placement to remove dust or packaging residue.</li>
        <li>Final placement is inspected by the site manager, who signs off on the placement checklist confirming that the furniture is level, stable, and free of blemishes.</li>
    </ul>
</li>

<li><strong>Swift removal of packing debris</strong>
